   369	  // F1 (pass 39): when the path carries NO method, Telegram falls back to the first `method` ARGUMENT.
   370	  // The door returned null for those and skipped every check, so a request to the token root carrying
   371	  // `method=sendMessage&text=<invisible>` dispatched normally and was never inspected. Recover the
   372	  // method from the parameters in exactly the case Telegram does.
