   416	        + 'reader-visible content is unknown and this request cannot be checked. Add it to '
   417	        + 'READER_VISIBLE_TELEGRAM_PARAMS (with its field) or to '
   418	        + 'NO_READER_VISIBLE_FIELD_TELEGRAM_METHODS (deliberately, having read the Bot API docs).',
   419	      );
   420	    }
   421	
   422	    const { params, uncheckable } = collectParams(href, checkedBody);
   423	    // F6 (pass 39): an unreadable body is only undecidable if the reader-visible field is not ALREADY
   424	    // supplied by the query — and query values win, so when one is present the body cannot change what
   425	    // Telegram sends. Refusing anyway destroyed a decidable, deliverable message.
   426	    // EVERY reader-visible field, not just the first: a method can carry more than one (pass 43), and
   427	    // an unreadable body is only harmless if the query already supplies ALL of them.
   428	    // The reader-visible fields of a method are ALTERNATIVES, not simultaneous requirements — a send
   429	    // carries `text` OR the rich structure. Requiring the query to supply ALL of them (pass 44) treated
   430	    // an either-or as an and, so my repair for one over-refusal introduced another one layer up.
   431	    //
   432	    // But ANY of them (pass 45's repair) was wrong in the other direction, and this is the third place
   433	    // today the same shape has bitten: the alternatives are a PRIORITY union, not a free choice.
   434	    // `editMessageText` reads `rich_message` whenever that key is present ANYWHERE in the request and
