  1421	        // DIFFERENT REPRESENTATION, and the post-format rule is precisely a claim about representation.
  1422	        // Malformed HTML with no text nodes has no reader-visible content AS HTML and is perfectly
  1423	        // visible as plain text — the retry shows the tags, which this path exists to do. Refusing it
  1424	        // outright destroyed a deliverable message, which the guard's own policy forbids.
  1425	        //
  1426	        // My sentence above ("retrying cannot make an invisible payload visible") was true of the rule
  1427	        // that existed when I wrote it and false of the rule I added an hour later. The two fixes
  1428	        // interacted, and only a reading that asked about the interaction found it.
